WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.271 --> 00:00:15.232
and Miles were put into a cell together.

2
00:00:17.213 --> 00:00:21.896
Edward stood at the bars, calling for the guard, while Miles sat sadly in a corner.

3
00:00:21.916 --> 00:00:25.018
"I demand to be released!"

4
00:00:25.418 --> 00:00:26.158
Edward shouted.

5
00:00:26.178 --> 00:00:28.940
"You have no right to imprison me!

6
00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:30.381
I'm the king!"

7
00:00:30.401 --> 00:00:34.323
"And I'm the emperor!"

8
00:00:34.724 --> 00:00:36.505
a prisoner in another cell shouted.

9
00:00:37.626 --> 00:00:39.907
There were roars of laughter from other prisoners.

10
00:00:46.932 --> 00:00:49.314
Edward went over to sit on the floor beside Miles.

11
00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:51.455
"How are you feeling?"

12
00:00:53.617 --> 00:00:54.417
Miles sighed.

13
00:00:54.437 --> 00:00:58.280
"I thought everyone at Hendon Hall would be happy to see me.

14
00:00:59.236 --> 00:01:03.099
Instead no one seemed to recognize me, and I wound up here.

15
00:01:03.119 --> 00:01:06.661
I don't know whether to laugh or cry."

16
00:01:08.242 --> 00:01:09.903
Edward put an arm around his friend.

17
00:01:09.923 --> 00:01:13.405
"You always get us out of trouble, Sir Miles.

18
00:01:14.746 --> 00:01:15.827
Maybe we can escape?"

19
00:01:17.988 --> 00:01:20.109
But Miles was too discouraged to try.

20
00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:23.752
He spent the rest of the day thinking about Edith.

21
00:01:27.324 --> 00:01:31.585
"I'm sure Edith recognized me," he said to Edward as they ate dinner.

22
00:01:31.605 --> 00:01:35.686
"But something—or someone—made her lie."

23
00:01:35.706 --> 00:01:39.207
"There's only one thing I'm sure of."

24
00:01:40.187 --> 00:01:43.388
Edward made a face as he swallowed a spoonful of brown glop.

25
00:01:44.489 --> 00:01:47.830
"This is the worst food I've ever tasted."

26
00:01:52.571 --> 00:01:56.772
The next day an old man carrying a basket came to visit all the prisoners.

27
00:01:58.496 --> 00:02:00.617
He handed fresh bread into each cell.

28
00:02:00.637 --> 00:02:03.337
"Blake Andrews!

29
00:02:03.677 --> 00:02:04.858
My former servant!"

30
00:02:05.298 --> 00:02:06.338
Miles cried happily.

31
00:02:06.358 --> 00:02:08.879
"You must recognize me!"

32
00:02:08.899 --> 00:02:14.360
"Shh!" Blake looked around to be sure no one was listening.

33
00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:17.341
"Thank goodness you've returned.

34
00:02:18.722 --> 00:02:23.183
I never believed you were dead, so when I heard you were here, I had to see for

35
00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:27.484
myself." Blake patted his basket of bread.

36
00:02:28.704 --> 00:02:31.725
"That's why I'm paying a charitable visit to the prisoners."

37
00:02:31.745 --> 00:02:34.326
"Clever man!"

38
00:02:34.827 --> 00:02:36.947
Miles reached through the bars for some bread.

39
00:02:36.967 --> 00:02:40.489
"Now tell me what's been going on."

40
00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:47.472
Blake explained that soon after Miles' brother Arthur died, Sir Richard became ill.

41
00:02:47.492 --> 00:02:53.314
"When your father received the letter about your death, he lost his will to live.

42
00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:58.336
He urged Hugh and Edith to marry before he passed away."

43
00:03:00.444 --> 00:03:02.285
"And she obviously agreed to that."

44
00:03:03.385 --> 00:03:04.965
Miles shook his head sadly.

45
00:03:04.985 --> 00:03:09.086
"No, she didn't!"

46
00:03:09.166 --> 00:03:11.467
Blake flashed Miles a triumphant smile.

47
00:03:11.487 --> 00:03:19.029
"She always believed that you'd return, so she resisted your father and Hugh's attempts to set a wedding

48
00:03:19.069 --> 00:03:23.610
date." Now it was Miles' turn to smile brightly.

49
00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:25.831
"That's my Edith!"

50
00:03:27.812 --> 00:03:29.352
Edward broke off a piece of bread.

51
00:03:30.616 --> 00:03:33.417
"So, how did she end up marrying Hugh?"

52
00:03:33.437 --> 00:03:41.000
"She finally gave in when Sir Richard was on his deathbed," Blake said.

53
00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:44.742
"And she's been unhappy ever since."

54
00:03:44.762 --> 00:03:47.963
"Oh, my darling Edith!"

55
00:03:48.583 --> 00:03:49.504
Miles whispered.

56
00:03:51.144 --> 00:03:53.725
Blake leaned close to the bars and spoke softly.

57
00:03:53.745 --> 00:04:00.108
"It's rumored that after the wedding, she found a rough draft of that letter in Hugh's desk.

58
00:04:01.416 --> 00:04:08.118
She accused Hugh of rushing the wedding—and causing Sir Richard's death—by writing the letter himself."

59
00:04:08.138 --> 00:04:12.579
"I can believe that," Edward said.

60
00:04:12.599 --> 00:04:21.942
"As soon as Sir Richard died, Hugh began treating everyone cruelly— the servants, the villagers, anyone who depended

61
00:04:22.022 --> 00:04:22.602
upon him."

62
00:04:23.683 --> 00:04:25.203
Blake hesitated for a moment.

63
00:04:25.223 --> 00:04:27.484
"Even Edith."

64
00:04:28.912 --> 00:04:33.075
This was too much for Miles, who grabbed the cell bars and tried to shake them.

65
00:04:33.095 --> 00:04:37.039
"I'll rescue Edith, if it's the last thing I do!"

66
00:04:39.861 --> 00:04:43.203
The next day Blake returned with more bread and more news.

67
00:04:43.223 --> 00:04:47.987
"The king will be crowned later this week," Blake said.

68
00:04:49.668 --> 00:04:51.410
Edward pulled on Miles' sleeve.

69
00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:54.092
"We have to go back to the city right now!"

70
00:04:56.432 --> 00:05:01.456
"I've heard that the king has an illness that affects his mind," Blake went on.

71
00:05:03.138 --> 00:05:04.639
Edward glared at the old man.

72
00:05:04.659 --> 00:05:07.602
"The king is in perfectly good health!

73
00:05:09.023 --> 00:05:11.865
I command you to stop this gossip right now!"

74
00:05:13.827 --> 00:05:15.248
Blake gestured toward Edward.

75
00:05:15.268 --> 00:05:17.730
"What's the boy talking about?"

76
00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:20.152
Miles shook his head.

77
00:05:20.172 --> 00:05:22.054
"It's not important."

78
00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:28.081
"Well, at least the king is kind and merciful," Blake said.

79
00:05:28.101 --> 00:05:33.903
"He spared the Duke of Norfolk's life, and now he's abolishing laws that oppress the poor."

80
00:05:33.923 --> 00:05:37.684
"Who is this king?"

81
00:05:38.284 --> 00:05:39.004
Edward thought.

82
00:05:39.024 --> 00:05:45.826
"Even if Tom tried to pass himself off as me, he couldn't keep up that act for long."

83
00:05:47.867 --> 00:05:51.808
Blake returned to the subject of the coronation and said Hugh would be attending.

84
00:05:52.876 --> 00:05:57.039
"He hopes the king will make him an earl because Hugh is friends with Lord Hertford."

85
00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:01.102
Edward started at the name of his adviser.

86
00:06:01.122 --> 00:06:03.403
"We'll see about that!"

87
00:06:03.844 --> 00:06:04.324
he said.

88
00:06:06.445 --> 00:06:09.508
After Blake left, two more prisoners were put into the cell.

89
00:06:11.029 --> 00:06:16.312
When Edward learned they were wrongly accused of crimes and sentenced to death, he was outraged.

90
00:06:16.332 --> 00:06:21.576
"Miles, we have to get to the coronation," he whispered excitedly.

91
00:06:22.672 --> 00:06:27.056
"After I'm crowned, I can pardon these men and save their lives!"

92
00:06:28.837 --> 00:06:30.198
Miles patted Edward's head.

93
00:06:30.218 --> 00:06:37.644
"First Blake's stories," he thought, "and now these fellows' tales of woe.

94
00:06:39.125 --> 00:06:42.568
I'm afraid everyone's stories have made Edward's illness worse!"
